  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "What RAG Is and the Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "What RAG Is and the Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What RAG Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RAG== = retrieve relevant text at **query time**, put it in the prompt",
                "The LLM answers **from that text**",
                "Model weights stay ==unchanged==",
                "Fresh or private facts come in through the prompt"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Two phases",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Offline ingestion",
                    "note": "load, clean, chunk, embed, index",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Online query",
                    "note": "embed query, retrieve, rerank, assemble, generate",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. RAG vs the Alternatives",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "RAG",
                "Fine-tuning",
                "Long context"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Gives",
                  "fresh or private facts",
                  "style, format, skill",
                  "everything, every time"
                ],
                [
                  "Cites sources",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "only if prompted"
                ],
                [
                  "Facts reliable",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "degrades mid-prompt"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost per query",
                  "small prompt",
                  "small prompt",
                  "{red:high, slower}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fine-tuning changes ==behavior==, not reliable facts",
                "Stuffing everything costs more, slows responses, loses details ==in the middle==",
                "Retrieval keeps the prompt **small**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mental Model",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Ceiling rule",
              "items": [
                "Answer quality is ==capped by retrieval quality==",
                "The LLM is only as right as the chunks it receives"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Wrong answer? Check the **retrieved chunks** first, before blaming the model or the prompt."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Chunking Strategies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Chunking Strategies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Chunk Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==chunk== is the unit that gets **embedded** and **retrieved**",
                "{red:Too big}: embedding is diluted, many topics blur into one vector",
                "{red:Too small}: context is lost, the fact has no surroundings"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Splitting Methods",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "How it splits",
                "Catch"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fixed-size",
                  "every ==500 tokens==",
                  "cuts sentences and ideas mid-way"
                ],
                [
                  "Recursive",
                  "paragraph, then sentence, then word",
                  "usual **default**"
                ],
                [
                  "Structure-aware",
                  "headings, code blocks, table rows",
                  "needs structured source"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Recursive split",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Paragraph",
                    "note": "try first",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sentence",
                    "note": "if still too big",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Word",
                    "note": "last resort",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Overlap and Metadata",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Overlap ==10-20%==: 500 tokens with 50-100 overlap",
                "Facts on a boundary are not lost",
                "Cost: a **larger index**",
                "Attach ==source, title, section, date== to every chunk"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Start with ==recursive split + 10-20% overlap + metadata on every chunk==; go structure-aware for docs, code and tables."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Embeddings and Indexing",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Embeddings and Indexing",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Embeddings",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An ==embedding== maps text to a **dense vector**",
                "Similar meaning gives ==nearby vectors==",
                "Similarity: {blue:cosine} or {blue:dot product}",
                "Embed docs and queries with the ==same model==",
                "New model means ==re-embed the whole corpus=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Flat vs ANN Search",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Index",
                "How it works",
                "Trade-off",
                "Tune"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Flat** (exact)",
                  "Compares every vector",
                  "Perfect recall, slow at scale",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "**HNSW**",
                  "Graph-based ANN",
                  "High recall, fast, ==heavy memory==",
                  "`ef_search`"
                ],
                [
                  "**IVF**",
                  "Clusters vectors, searches nearest clusters only",
                  "Less memory, may miss edge clusters",
                  "`nprobe`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**ANN** trades a little ==recall== for big speed gains",
                "Higher `ef_search` / `nprobe` means more recall, more latency"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Vector DB and Filters",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Query vector",
                    "sub": "same model",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata filter",
                    "sub": "tenant, date, doc type",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ANN search",
                    "sub": "HNSW or IVF",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Top-k chunks",
                    "sub": "with metadata",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Store vectors plus metadata in `pgvector`, Pinecone, Qdrant or OpenSearch",
                "Filter ==before or during== search, not after"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Mixing embedding models gives **meaningless similarity**. A filter applied after top-k can leave you with {red:too few results}."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hybrid Search and Reranking",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Hybrid Search and Reranking",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. BM25 vs Vectors",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "BM25",
                "Vectors"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Scores by",
                  "term frequency + rarity",
                  "meaning similarity"
                ],
                [
                  "Wins on",
                  "==IDs==, error codes, names",
                  "paraphrase, synonyms"
                ],
                [
                  "Misses",
                  "reworded text",
                  "exact rare tokens"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Hybrid Search and RRF",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Query",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "BM25 + vector",
                    "sub": "in parallel",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Two ranked lists",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RRF merge",
                    "sub": "one list",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RRF== score = sum of `1/(k+rank)` over every list; **k is about 60**",
                "Uses ranks only, so {green:no score normalization} needed",
                "Docs high in both lists rise to the top"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Retrieve Wide, Then Rerank",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Retrieve",
                    "note": "top 50-100, cheap",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cross-encoder rerank",
                    "note": "score each query-doc pair",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Keep top 3-8",
                    "note": "to the prompt",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Bi-encoder",
                "Cross-encoder"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Reads",
                  "query and doc ==separately==",
                  "query + doc ==together=="
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "fast, scales to corpus",
                  "too slow for whole corpus"
                ],
                [
                  "Accuracy",
                  "good",
                  "higher"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Cheap and wide first, accurate and narrow second: a cross-encoder only ever sees the shortlist."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
